      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-311318",
      ":question/problem": "$S = 2(3x \\cdot x + 3x \\cdot 5 + x \\cdot 5)$\nThe length of a container's base is $3$ times its width $x$, and the height of the container is $5$ inches. The function $S$, given above, models the surface area of the container as a rectangular solid, expressed in square inches. Which expression represents the area of the container's base, in square inches?"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186217563,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/type": {
