      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-311647",
      ":question/problem": "A right rectangular prism has a height of $12$ centimeters. The length of the prism's base is $x$ centimeters, which is $3$ centimeters more than the width of the prism's base. Which function $V$ gives the volume of the prism, in cubic centimeters, in terms of the length of the prism's base, where $x > 3$?"
